--- answer ---
Cause: `removeOldest` (simplelru/lru.go:170) removes `c.evictList.Front()` — the **front** of the list is where new/updated entries are pushed (lru.go:53,59), i.e. the most recently used end. The oldest entry is at the **back** (`RemoveOldest`, `GetOldest`, and `Keys` all treat `Back()` as oldest). So a full cache evicted the MRU entry.Fixed: `removeOldest` in simplelru/lru.go:170 was evicting `evictList.Front()` (the MRU end, where entries are pushed) instead of `evictList.Back()` (the LRU end, consistent with `RemoveOldest`/`GetOldest`/`Keys`). Changed it to `Back()`. Build, vet, and the full test suite all pass.